WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:09.200
For stand leads. After the game, you check everyone against the paper sign-in sheet, and send it in. It takes about five minutes.

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:17.133
On game day, it's at the top of your volunteer page. Tap Log your stand's hours. The link is in your Hub email too.

00:00:17.333 --> 00:00:21.270
Page not working? Text tech support, right from here.

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:26.387
Need to reach your crew? Text everyone working opens one group text.

00:00:26.587 --> 00:00:30.300
After the game, check each person against the paper sign-in sheet.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:34.140
If your whole stand moved, change Stand worked here.

00:00:34.990 --> 00:00:38.191
Each worker has a card, with Call and Text buttons.

00:00:38.391 --> 00:00:41.165
Fix their time in and time out to match the sheet.

00:00:41.365 --> 00:00:44.459
Check who their hours count for: the student's full name,

00:00:44.659 --> 00:00:46.480
and the program.

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:49.805
Someone didn't come? Pick Did not show up.

00:00:50.005 --> 00:00:56.310
Someone else worked a person's shift? Tap Someone else worked this shift, and type who actually worked.

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:59.251
Extra spots ask who worked them.

00:00:59.451 --> 00:01:03.697
Someone worked who wasn't on the sign-up? Tap Add someone who wasn't on SignUp.

00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:10.050
Then take one clear photo of the paper sign-in sheet. You can save a copy to your phone, too.

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:14.186
Enter your name. You get an email copy, with the photo.

00:01:14.386 --> 00:01:20.350
Tap Submit for approval. Hours are added after the IU liaison approves them.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:26.780
Done! Need to fix something? Open the same link, and resubmit before it's approved.

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:35.980
Want to practice first? Ask the IU liaison for the practice stand page. It works the same way, and nothing on it counts.
